g a period, while cash-basis shows what cash moved. Accrual gives a clearer picture of ongoing profitability; cash-basis makes it easier to track short-term cash flow. Small operations often use cash-basis for simplicity; businesses that need a fuller view of performance usually use accrual. I did not consult external sources for this reply—tell me if you’d like formal citations or brief examples and I’ll fetch them.","runId":"run_8ee19264edba3cc9","sampleIndex":0,"schemaVersion":"2.0.0","status":"completed","strategy":"compiler_slice","structuralRetention":{"allArtifactCriticalPoliciesRetained":true,"criticalPolicyIds":["universal_honesty","no_hidden_reasoning_reveal","no_background_work_claims","do_not_mention_internal_policy","do_not_invent_facts","no_raw_tool_json_exposure","privacy_floor","authoritative_sources_preferred"],"selectedPolicyIds":["universal_honesty","no_hidden_reasoning_reveal","no_background_work_claims","do_not_mention_internal_policy","do_not_invent_facts","no_raw_tool_json_exposure","privacy_floor","citations_required","authoritative_sources_preferred","citation_definition"]},"toolCalls":[],"toolCostUsd":0.0,"totalTokens":6462,"trialId":"trial_785c89fcc6e5b45d"}
